        "content": "<p>Hi, I was reading the Monad Map in the <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/wiki/Monad-map/406b6e8101a7c0e8ab9bffc122d12a7965845220\">mathlib wiki</a></p>\n<p>In the very first line, it says </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">solid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arrow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">upwards</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">means</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"when in the A Monad, anything in B can be</span>\n<span class=\"s2\">called directly\"</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">there</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lift</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">If</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arrow</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">labeled</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">you</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">must</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">call</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">that</span>\n<span class=\"n\">function</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">so</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I am confused here, if we are lifting from B to A, shouldnt the arrow be from B to A insteaf of A to B??<br>\nAs it says, when in A monad(lower level), anything in B can be called directly. But doesnt the latter part means A is more powerful/superset of B. This feels a bit inconsistent to me.<br>\nCould anyone clarify if I am mistaken in my concepts. Thanks</p>",
